- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`ContentstackFactory`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack object is instantiated (line 87, confirmed by tool). Live Preview requires the Stack initialization to include live_preview config (enable:true, preview_host), and the query helpers (getEntry, getSingleEntry, etc.) that call setCommonConfig/createContentTypeQuery must forward live_preview tokens from the CMS URL. All 4 callers of ContentstackFactory are in this same file, making it the single point where preview is wired into every content query.
  - **Minimal fix:** In ContentstackFactory, add live_preview configuration to the Stack initialization: pass live_preview: { enable: true, host: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST } (or equivalent env var). Then in setCommonConfig (called by createContentTypeQuery and createContentTypeEntryQuery), include .livePreviewQuery(requestParams) or manually add the live_preview token/hash from the incoming request query params so that every content query forwards preview context. This is the minimal change — one config block in the factory and one query-param forward in the shared config setter — that enables live preview across all 236+ useContent consumers without touching any presentation code.


